/-!
# Freezing the expanding-eigenline transverse energy

The finite-sector Parseval bridge controls the exact Fourier misalignment by
energy transverse to one frozen expanding strain eigenline.  This module
quantifies the change in that transverse energy when the expanding eigenline
varies.

The argument is sign invariant.  It compares rank-one line projectors, not
chosen eigenvectors.  Away from a spectral collision, the existing matched
eigenline perturbation theorem gives a `4 * epsilon / gap` error.  Near a
collision the theorem returns the collision branch explicitly.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

noncomputable section

namespace Mettapedia
namespace FluidDynamics
namespace NavierStokes
namespace PancakeTransverseEnergyFreezing

open MeasureTheory
open scoped RealInnerProductSpace
open PeriodicFourierTriad
open PancakeAlignmentDynamics
open PancakeComplexMisalignmentExpansion
